  "historical_output_text": " I was quite the klutz in my younger years, always knocking things over or spilling something on myself. One day, I was rushing to get ready for a job interview. In a hurry, I tripped and spilled coffee all over my shirt. I felt mortified, but instead of panicking, I paused and took a few deep breaths.\n\nI quickly realized the coffee was still hot, so I ran under the cold water tap to cool it. Then I grabbed some t-shirts from my dresser and tried them on, finding a clean one that fit. I quickly redid my hair and put on some deodorant. \n\nWhen I arrived at the interview, the smell of the coffee lingered on me, but I was able to carry myself with poise and confidence. Afterwards, I learned it's better to stay calm and method",
